          than a preference. /map/rate-parity.svg is an ENDPOINT: it is rebuilt from the data
          on every build, so it cannot go stale. The PNGs are committed artifacts generated by
          scripts/build-parity-png.py, so they can. The block says so out loud, because a
          writer choosing a file should know which one is guaranteed current, and because
          telling them is cheaper than a stale PNG in somebody's article.

          THE CSV CARRIES PUBLISHED FIELDS ONLY. Five columns, every one already visible on
